  "content": {
    "title": "MLB Opening Night: Yankees thump Giants behind Max Fried's gem for fifth straight season-opening win",
    "text": "The 2026 MLB season has begun, and the New York Yankees are 1-0.The Yankees opened the season with a 7-0 win over the San Francisco Giants, taking a lead early and coasting from there behind 6 1/3 shutout innings from starting pitcher Max Fried. It is New York’s fifth straight Opening Day victory.AdvertisementFacing Giants ace Logan Webb, the Yankees pounced in the second inning, with six straight hits to take a 5-0 lead. Trent Grisham, playing his first game since returning to the team on a qualifying offer last winter, capped the rally with a triple.Two more runs followed in the fifth inning, enough to raise Webb’s ERA to 10.80. His six earned runs were more than he allowed in any start in 2025.Every member of the Yankees’ lineup finished the game with a hit, save for one. Reigning AL MVP Aaron Judge went 0-for-5 with four strikeouts, marking the first time since 2024 that he posted that many strikeouts in a game.AdvertisementYankees shortstop José Caballero also became a part of history when he was the first player to challenge a pitch using MLB’s new ABS challenge system in the fourth inning. He challenged the strike call on the first pitch of the fourth inning and lost.Here’s how Yankees-Giants unfolded in real-time on Opening Night:Live coverage is over39 updatesThu, March 26, 2026 at 12:05 AM UTCThu, March 26, 2026 at 3:00 AM UTCThu, March 26, 2026 at 2:55 AM UTCThe Giants cannot score a run, as it turns out.The Yankees deliver a resounding Opening Night win behind 6 1/3 dominant innings from Fried and a well-rounded offensive effort.These two teams will play again on Friday.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:53 AM UTCAdames reaches on a fielding error to lead off the bottom of the frame.He goes to second on a wild pitch and to third on a groundout. Can the Giants score a run?Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:46 AM UTCYankees go down without making any noise, and it’s on to the Giants’ last three chances in this game.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:41 AM UTCJudge grounds out to begin the 9th. Rough night at the office for him, though at least he didn’t strike out 5 times.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:40 AM UTCDevers flies out, and the Giants’ are still scoreless through 8. On to the 9th!Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:38 AM UTCWith Max Fried finally out of the game, the Giants have gotten some action on the basepaths in the 8th. Luis Arraez singled for the team’s third hit of the game, and Matt Chapman drew a walk.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:33 AM UTCYankees go down 1-2-3 in the 8th. Giants have 6 more outs to avoid a shutout in their home opener.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:25 AM UTCJack BaerJake Bird quickly finishes off the seventh inning, and it’s still all Yankees. To the eighth we go.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:20 AM UTCJack BaerCody Bellinger lines out and that will do it for Max Fried at 86 pitches. His full line: 6 1/3 innings, 2 hits, 0 runs, 1 walk, 4 strikeouts.In comes Jake Bird for the Yankees.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:18 AM UTCJack BaerJT Brubaker keeps the top of the seventh scoreless with a double play from José Caballero. Max Fried is back out there for a seventh inning against a Giants lineup he’s dominated so far.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:03 AM UTCJack BaerAaron Judge has four strikeouts tonight. That's the first time since 2024 that he's struck out four times in a game.— Chris Kirschner (@ChrisKirschner) March 26, 2026Thu, March 26, 2026 at 2:02 AM UTCJack BaerKeaton Winn relieves the struggling Logan Webb and works around a leadoff walk. In the process, he ensured that Aaron Judge has officially started the 2026 MLB season with a golden sombrero.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 1:52 AM UTCJack BaerMeanwhile, Max Fried is still cruising. Another 1-2-3 inning in the fifth while holding a seven-run lead.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 1:47 AM UTCWebb has a 10.80 ERA after 5 innings to begin the 2026 season. He has thrown 86 pitches, recorded 7 strikeouts and allowed 6 earned runs.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 1:44 AM UTCJack BaerThe top of the 5th is not going any better for Logan Webb. Three straight singles followed by a forceout with a throwing error have made it 7-0 New York.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 1:39 AM UTCJack BaerNetflix’s scorebug has been drawing a mixed reaction online.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 1:36 AM UTCJack BaerMax Fried has struck out four, walked one and allowed only two hits in four shutout innings so far. He’s at 64 pitches.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 1:30 AM UTCJack BaerLogan Webb got in some more trouble on a Ryan McMahon walk and Austin Wells single, but he escapes by striking out Aaron Judge for the third time tonight. 71 pitches through four innings for him, and that was also the 1,000th strikeout of his career.Thu, March 26, 2026 at 1:29 AM UTCJack Baer",
